Embalm is a shaman ritual that preserves corpses from the natural process
of decay. Through communion with the spirits of preservation, the shaman
can extend the time a corpse remains intact.

Usage: cast 'embalm' <corpse>

This spell requires a corpse as the target. When successfully cast, the
corpse's decay timer is significantly extended, giving more time to
retrieve belongings, perform burial rites, or conduct other activities
that require an intact body.

Embalm is a tasked spell that requires concentration to complete. The
spell has no effect on corpses that are already immune to decay.

Class: Shaman
Discipline: Shaman

